{"name":"Vacation Island","hex":"#d1d991","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vacation","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An extended trip or journey away from home for rest or pleasure. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","An extended period of leisure time away from work or school."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spend or take a vacation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vacation"},{"term":"island","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A contiguous area of land, smaller than a continent, totally surrounded by water.","A contiguous area of land, smaller than a continent, partially surrounded by water; a peninsula; a half-island."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To surround with water; make into an island.","To set, dot (as if) with islands."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/island"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vacation","blocks":[{"text":"A vacation or holiday is either a leave of absence from a regular job or school or an instance of leisure travel away from home. People often take a vacation during specific holiday observances or for specific festivals or celebrations. Vacations are often spent with friends or family. Vacations may include a specific trip or journey, usually for the purpose of recreation or tourism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Vacation_Village_at_Weston_Pool%2C_Weston%2C_Florida_February_24%2C_2022_B.jpg/330px-Vacation_Village_at_Weston_Pool%2C_Weston%2C_Florida_February_24%2C_2022_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vacation","wikidata":"Q116213"},{"title":"Island","blocks":[{"text":"An island or isle is a piece of land, distinct from a continent, completely surrounded by water. There are continental islands, which were formed by being split from a continent by plate tectonics, and oceanic islands, which have never been part of a continent. Oceanic islands can be formed from volcanic activity, grow into atolls from coral reefs, and form from sediment along shorelines, creating barrier islands. River islands can also form from sediment and debris in rivers. Artificial islands are those made by humans, including small rocky outcroppings built out of lagoons and large-scale land reclamation projects used for development."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg/330px-Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Island","wikidata":"Q23442"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png/500px-Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png/1280px-Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png/500px-Days-of-vacation-and-holidays.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Average number of vacation days over time in various countries","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADays-of-vacation-and-holidays.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Vacation_research_design.jpg/500px-Vacation_research_design.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Vacation_research_design.jpg/1280px-Vacation_research_design.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Vacation_research_design.jpg/500px-Vacation_research_design.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pa